><EXTERNAL_ID namespace="GEO">GSE246309</EXTERNAL_ID></IDENTIFIERS><DESCRIPTOR><STUDY_TITLE>Genomic regions occupied by both RARa and VDR are involved in the convergence and cooperation of retinoid and vitamin D signaling pathways.</STUDY_TITLE><STUDY_TYPE existing_study_type="Transcriptome Analysis"/><STUDY_ABSTRACT>In this study, the retinoid and vitamin D pathways were investigated in PMA-differentiated THP-1 cells treated with or without the RARa agonist, AM580, and/or the VDR agonist, 1,25-dihydroxyvitamin D3 (1,25-vitD or calcitriol), using global approaches. Binding regions of RARa and VDR were determined in PMA-differentiated THP-1 cells using chromatin immunoprecipitation coupled with high-throughput sequencing (ChIP-seq). The gene sets regulated by AM580 and/or 1,25-vitD were identified by RNA-sequencing (RNA-seq). The activity of the regulatory regions was determined by MED1 (a subunit of the Mediator complex) ChIP-seq and chromatin openness was measured using assay for transposase-accessible chromatin with sequencing (ATAC-seq). Overall design: THP1 cells were stimulated with 20 nM PMA for 16 hours. PMA-differentiated THP-1 cells were treated with vehicle (DMSO:EtOH), RARa agonist (100 nM AM580) and/or VDR agonist (100 nM calcitriol or 1,25-vitD) for 6 hours. Three replicates of each condition were analyzed by RNA-seq.</STUDY_ABSTRACT><CENTER_PROJECT_NAME>GSE246309</CENTER_PROJECT_NAME></DESCRIPTOR><STUDY_LINKS><STUDY_LINK><XREF_LINK><DB>pubmed</DB><ID>40167329</ID></XREF_LINK></STUDY_LINK></STUDY_LINKS><STUDY_ATTRIBUTES><STUDY_ATTRIBUTE><TAG>parent_bioproject</TAG><VALUE>PRJNA1032473</VALUE></STUDY_ATTRIBUTE></STUDY_ATTRIBUTES></STUDY><SAMPLE alias="GSM7866526" accession="SRS19294211"><IDENTIFIERS><PRIMARY_ID>SRS19294211</PRIMARY_ID><EXTERNAL_ID namespace="BioSample">SAMN37998447</EXTERNAL_ID><EXTERNAL_ID namespace="GEO">GSM7866526</EXTERNAL_ID></IDENTIFIERS><TITLE>PMA-stimulated THP1 cells, 6h, vehicle (DMSO:EtOH), replicate 1</TITLE><SAMPLE_NAME><TAXO